cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Verifiable Geocomputation: Formal Specification, Machine-Checked Proofs and Autonomous Reasoning for DEM Terrain Analysis"
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Verifiable Geocomputation is an open research programme that brings formal
  verification from AI theorem proving into geospatial analysis. It asks whether
  the verifiability of spatial computing results can be formally defined, proved,
  and machine-checked, and builds three layers of assets: VeriGIS (a formally
  specified operator library), GeoProofBench (a benchmark of formal propositions
  for DEM spatial reasoning), and GeoMath-Agent (an autonomous agent for
  spatial theorem proving).

